{
  "dom_id": "step-q148051",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "What is the missing number?\n\n$\\,$ $\\boxed{}\\,%$ of $25=40$",
  "worked_solution": "We can write the given problem as the following product:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%\\times 25=40\n$$\n\nUsing the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%=40÷25=\\frac{40}{25}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{40}{25}=\\frac{40\\times 4}{25\\times 4}=\\frac{160}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{160}{100}=160%\n$$",
